From: CapCut-on-Wine project
Subject: wbemdisp: implement the SWbemDateTime (ISWbemDateTime) scripting object

SYMPTOM
  CapCut PC logs, immediately followed by whatever component asked for the class:

      err:ole:com_get_class_object class {47dfbe54-cf76-11d3-b38f-00105a1f473a} not registered
      err:ole:com_get_class_object no class object {47dfbe54-cf76-11d3-b38f-00105a1f473a}
      could be created for context 0x1

  {47DFBE54-CF76-11D3-B38F-00105A1F473A} is CLSID_SWbemDateTime (WbemScripting.SWbemDateTime,
  IID_ISWbemDateTime {5E97458A-CF77-11D3-B38F-00105A1F473A}, wbemdisp.dll / wbemdisp.tlb) -- the
  WMI scripting helper that converts the CIM DATETIME string (yyyymmddHHMMSS.mmmmmm+UUU) to and
  from VT_DATE and FILETIME.  Wine implements the rest of the WMI scripting objects (SWbemLocator,
  SWbemServices, SWbemObject, SWbemObjectSet, ...) but not this one, so any
  CoCreateInstance(CLSID_SWbemDateTime) fails with REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG.

CLASSIFICATION
  GENERAL WINE GAP FOUND WHILE MAKING CAPCUT RUN, NOT A CAPCUT-EXCLUSIVE HACK.  The class is
  absent from every Wine version (searched wine-11.18, our patched tree and /opt/wine-staging: no
  CLSID, no interface, no symbol), and any WMI-scripting consumer hits the same
  REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG.  It is therefore part of the shared series, not of patches/local/.

CHANGE
  * include/wbemdisp.idl: add interface ISWbemDateTime (the full Microsoft surface: Value,
    Year/YearSpecified, Month/MonthSpecified, Day/DaySpecified, Hours/HoursSpecified,
    Minutes/MinutesSpecified, Seconds/SecondsSpecified, Microseconds/MicrosecondsSpecified,
    UTC/UTCSpecified, IsInterval, and GetVarDate/SetVarDate/GetFileTime/SetFileTime) and
    coclass SWbemDateTime, so widl registers the CLSID/ProgID and builds the typelib entry the
    object's IDispatch implementation needs.
  * dlls/wbemdisp/datetime.c: new file implementing the object and the conversions:
      - the object stores the timestamp components plus the CIM offset and the '*' specified
        flags; the internal instant is (components - offset), rendered in UTC or local time;
      - Value <-> components round trip, including interval form
        (ddddddddHHMMSS.mmmmmm:000, the leading 8 digits are the day count) and '*' wildcards
        for fields whose *Specified flag is FALSE;
      - GetVarDate/SetVarDate (VARIANT DATE), GetFileTime/SetFileTime (FILETIME as a decimal
        BSTR), both honouring the local/UTC flag through the machine time zone;
      - error codes measured on Windows: WBEM_E_INVALID_SYNTAX (0x80041021) for a malformed or
        out-of-range-for-conversion value, WBEM_E_VALUE_OUT_OF_RANGE (0x8004102b) for an
        out-of-range component assignment, WBEM_E_FAILED (0x80041001) for GetVarDate/GetFileTime
        on an interval or with unspecified components.
  * dlls/wbemdisp/main.c, wbemdisp_private.h, locator.c: wire the new CLSID into DllGetClassObject
    and share the existing typelib helper (get_typeinfo) with the new object.
  * dlls/wbemdisp/tests/wbemdisp.c: cover create-via-CoCreateInstance, Value<->VT_DATE for a UTC
    and an offset timestamp, IsInterval, interval parsing/building, GetFileTime/SetFileTime round
    trip, and malformed input.

  Conversions were measured against Windows 11 (build 26200, time zone Pacific) running the real
  wbemdisp.dll:  Value "20000120195632.000000-480" -> GetVarDate(false) 2000-01-21 03:56:32 UTC,
  GetVarDate(true) 2000-01-20 19:56:32 local;  interval GetVarDate/GetFileTime -> 0x80041001;
  put_Value("garbage") -> 0x80041021 leaving the object unchanged;  put_Month(13) -> 0x8004102b.

